    "body": "LOGICAL_OWNER = JINGO\nROLE = SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE / AUTOMATION\nSTATE = DESIGN PROPOSED / IMPLEMENTATION NOT STARTED\n\n## PURPOSE\nRemove manual PowerShell/operator relay from the ZB agent workflow while preserving truthful durable state and existing SALVADOR production locks.\n\n## ROOT CAUSE\nThe current controller already supports continuous `run_forever()` polling, but deployment has remained `--once`/manual. There is also no transport from ChatGPT attachments to the owner-PC inbox.\n\n## DECOMPOSITION\nThis umbrella contains two independent subprojects and they MUST NOT be merged into one implementation blob:\n\n### A. CONTROLLER DAEMON v1 — FIRST\nGoal: owner logs into Windows and the controller starts automatically, stays alive, restarts on failure, uses existing GitHub auth/config, and polls without manual PowerShell.\nRecommended deployment: Windows Task Scheduler + user-session daemon + watchdog/restart policy.\nReason: ComfyUI and `gh` auth are already user-session resources; native Windows Service adds admin/credential/desktop coupling without v1 value.\n\n### B. REFERENCE BRIDGE v1 — SECOND\nGoal: a ChatGPT-uploaded image can reach the correct `D:\\BLATT2\\ZB_AGENT_INBOX\\<TASK_ID>\\` without manual file copying.\nPreferred transport candidate: ChatGPT -> connected Google Drive drop folder -> Google Drive Desktop/local sync -> validated local bridge -> task inbox.\nThis requires a separate feasibility/transport gate before implementation.\n\n## BASELINE\nSALVADOR production controller authority remains exact HEAD `425ad97c508c4f55f7d7052435a7a2cb4aa3b015` on branch `agent-controller/salvador-v1-task8-repair`.\nDo not modify SALVADOR model/profile/workflow/prompt/denoise/dimensions.\nDo not merge Babylon work into this stream.\n\n## CONTROLLER DAEMON v1 DESIGN DIRECTION\n- start automatically at Windows user logon;\n- run `python -m zb_local_controller --config <production-config>` WITHOUT `--once`;\n- one instance only;\n- no duplicate controller process;\n- restart automatically after crash/non-zero exit;\n- write local health/status log and PID/instance evidence;\n- fail closed if config/GitHub auth is invalid;\n- no silent task-state fabrication;\n- existing `ASSIGNED != RUNNING`, `RUNNING` requires real prompt id, `RESULT_READY` requires real bytes/provenance remain unchanged;\n- install/uninstall/status scripts are idempotent;\n- no admin privilege required for normal v1 install if Windows permits current-user scheduled task;\n- owner can stop/disable it explicitly;\n- no production task auto-creation by daemon itself; it only consumes valid GitHub tasks.\n\n## OUT OF SCOPE FOR DAEMON v1\n- Windows native service/NSSM/pywin32 service;\n- tray UI;\n- remote desktop control;\n- model management;\n- ComfyUI auto-update;\n- SALVADOR profile changes;\n- reference-file transport;\n- Babylon integration;\n- canon mutation.\n\n## REQUIRED GATES\n1. OWNER DESIGN APPROVAL — daemon v1.\n2. Formal spec.\n3. OWNER SPEC REVIEW.\n4. Implementation plan.\n5. LESTER TDD implementation from exact approved base/plan.\n6. DUNCAN independent QC.\n7. Owner-PC live autostart/restart smoke.\n8. Only then mark daemon production active.\n9. After daemon lock, open Reference Bridge v1 transport feasibility/design gate.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION = NOT STARTED\nMERGE = NO\nPRODUCTION_ACTIVATION = NO\nCURRENT_FOCUS = CONTROLLER DAEMON v1\nOWNER_APPROVAL_PHRASE = APPROVE ZB CONTROLLER DAEMON V1 DESIGN",
